# SentinelC

A lightweight File Integrity Monitoring and Tamper Detection prototype written in C.

## About the Project

SentinelC is an academic C programming project focused on file integrity and tamper detection concepts.

The project uses a file record containing:

- Filename
- File size
- Hash value

It uses the FNV-1a 32-bit hashing algorithm to generate a hash value for demonstration.

## What I Learned

Through this project, I practiced:

- C structures
- Functions
- Arrays
- User input and output
- String handling
- Hashing concepts
- File integrity concepts
- Basic problem decomposition

## Current Scope

This repository contains an early prototype developed as part of my structured programming learning.

It is intended for educational purposes and does not claim to be a production-level file monitoring system.

